-- title:
--   Frobenius and Verschiebung on sections of a re-based rigidification
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $r$, a natural number $N$, and a characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain $\mathcal{O}$ with irreducible element $\pi$, complete for the $\pi$-adic topology, with $\#(\mathcal{O}/(\pi)) = r$ and $(r) = (\pi)$. Let $Onr$ be a characteristic-zero domain over $\mathcal{O}$ carrying an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra automorphism $Fr$, complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, with that ideal maximal, every element of $Onr$ satisfying a monic $\mathcal{O}$-polynomial modulo $\pi$, every monic polynomial of positive degree over $Onr$ having a root modulo $\pi$, and $Fr(x) \equiv x^{r} \pmod{\pi}$ for all $x$; write $k_0 = Onr/(\pi)$. Let $\Lambda \subseteq \mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule. Given fake elliptic curves $A_0, A_0^{(r)}$ of type $(\Lambda,N)$ over $k_0$ (schemes with a commutative relative group law, the abelian-scheme property bundle, two-dimensional fibres, a $\Lambda$-action and a level structure), a section $P_0$ of $A_0$ over $k_0$, and $prA : A_0^{(r)} \to A_0$ exhibiting $A_0^{(r)}$ as the pullback of $A_0$ along the map $k_0 \to k_0$ induced by $Fr$ (`IsPullbackVia`: a cartesian square compatible with the group laws, the $\Lambda$-action and the level structure), suppose $F : A_0 \to A_0^{(r)}$ and $V : A_0^{(r)} \to A_0$ are morphisms over $k_0$ that are homomorphisms on points, commute with the $\Lambda$-action, carry points factoring through the level structure to such points, satisfy $V \circ F = [r]$ and $F \circ V = [r]$ on points, and are such that for every commutative ring $C$ of characteristic $r$ and every $x : \operatorname{Spec} C \to A_0$ one has $x$ followed by $F$ followed by $prA$ equal to the absolute Frobenius of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ followed by $x$. Let $B$ be a nontrivial $\mathcal{O}$-algebra in which $\pi$ is nilpotent, $\psi : Onr \to B$ an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map, $E$ a fake elliptic curve over $B$, and $\rho$, $\rho^{+}$ rigidifications of $E$ relative to $A_0$ for $\psi$ and for the twist $\psi \circ Fr$ respectively (each consisting of the reduction $E_b$ over $B/(\pi)$ as pullback of $E$, a pullback $A_b$ of $A_0$ along the induced map of residue rings, and a degree-$r^{d}$ isogeny pair between $E_b$ and $A_b$ preserving the level structure). Assume further: a morphism $ub : \rho.E_b \to \rho^{+}.E_b$ compatible with the comparison maps $g_b$ and with the structure maps; a morphism $gA'$ exhibiting $\rho^{+}.A_b$ as the pullback of $A_0^{(r)}$ along the residue map induced by $\psi$, with $gA'$ followed by $prA$ equal to $\rho^{+}.gA$; and morphisms $F_b : \rho.A_b \to \rho^{+}.A_b$ and $V_b : \rho^{+}.A_b \to \rho.A_b$ over $B/(\pi)$ with $F_b$ followed by $gA'$ equal to $\rho.gA$ followed by $F$, and $V_b$ followed by $\rho.gA$ equal to $gA'$ followed by $V$. Finally let $Q$ and $Q^{+}$ be sections of $\rho.A_b$ and $\rho^{+}.A_b$ over $\operatorname{Spec}(B/(\pi))$ whose composites with $\rho.gA$, respectively $\rho^{+}.gA$, are $P_0$ pulled back along the residue map induced by $\psi$, respectively by $\psi \circ Fr$. Then $Q$ followed by $F_b$ equals $Q^{+}$, and $Q^{+}$ followed by $V_b$ equals the underlying morphism of the $r$-fold multiple of $Q$ for the group law of $\rho.A_b$ (the iterate `nsmulPt`).
--
--   This records the two point identities expressing that, after reduction modulo $\pi$, the comparison maps between a rigidification and its Frobenius re-basing act on the distinguished section as relative Frobenius and Verschiebung, the composite being multiplication by $r$. It is used in the identification of full level structures under norm-compatible transport for the Frobenius twist, within the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation of quaternionic Shimura curves.
